e}, {"t_ms": 29198, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "call_01a150ad01d673778483f6de", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 29964, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "call_01a150ad04db7367bb55c678", "tool": "get_service_status", "args": {"service": "payments-api"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 30264, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "call_01a150ad04db7367bb55c678", "tool": "get_service_status", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 30264, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "call_01a150ad04db7367bb55c678", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 31237, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "call_01a150ad089b7495ae02fd58", "tool": "create_incident", "args": {"idempotency_key": "payments-api-sev2-rollback-v5.1.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "payments-api", "summary": "Payments began throwing errors (~18% error rate) following this morning's deployment of v5.1.0 to all production regions. Rolled back to v5.0.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production. Rollback completed across us-east, us-west, and eu-west; service is now healthy with error rate down to ~0.2%. No approval needed: v5.0.0 was previously healthy in production. Recommend investigating v5.1.0 before redeploying.", "title": "Payments v5.1.0 deployment caused error spike; rolled back to v5.0.0"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 31837, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "call_01a150ad089b7495ae02fd58", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "payments-api-sev2-rollback-v5.1.0", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 31837, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "call_01a150ad089b7495ae02fd58", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 32838, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "Done. Here's a summary of what happened:\n\n1. **Identified the service** \u2014 \"payments\" wasn't a registered service name; the affected service is **payments-api**. It was on v5.1.0 in all regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west), unhealthy with an 18% error rate.\n\n2. **Found the last healthy release** \u2014 Deployment history showed v5.0.0 was healthy in production and v5.1.0 was degraded. Since v5.0.0 was previously healthy, no change-manager approval was required for the rollback.\n\n3. **Rolled back** \u2014 v5.0.0 was rolled out to all production regions and verified healthy, with the error rate down to ~0.2%.\n\n4. **Opened incident** \u2014 SEV2 incident **INC-0001** created for payments-api, documenting the error spike, the rollback to v5.0.0, and a recommendation to investigate v5.1.0 before redeploying. On-call has been paged.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"served_model": "zai-org/GLM-5.3-Flash", "system_fingerprint": "default", "finish_reason": "tool_calls", "content": "I'll start by checking the payments service status and its deployment history.", "reasoning_content": "Need to find payments service deployments and status. Let me check deployments first.", "tool_calls": [{"id": "call_01a150acaf917581aca0dbfe", "function": {"arguments": "{\"service\":\"payments\"}", "name": "get_service_status"}, "type": "function"}, {"id": "call_01a150acaf917581aca0dbff", "function": {"arguments": "{\"service\":\"payments\"}", "name": "list_deployments"}, "type": "function"}]}, {"served_model": "zai-org/GLM-5.3-Flash", "system_fingerprint": "default", "finish_reason": "tool_calls", "content": "The service \"payments\" wasn't found under that exact name. Let me try common naming variants and check incidents for clues about the correct service name.", "reasoning_content": "The service \"payments\" isn't found. Maybe named differently, e.g., \"payment-service\" or \"PaymentService\". I can't list services. Try a few variants? Maybe check incidents for context. Let me try \"payment-service\" and \"payment\".", "tool_calls": [{"id": "call_01a150acb38075b1b2d6c43f", "function": {"arguments": "{\"service\":\"payment-service\"}", "name": "get_service_status"}, "type": "function"}, {"id": "call_01a150acb38075b1b2d6c440", "function": {"arguments": "{}", "name": "list_incidents"}, "type": "function"}]}, {"served_model": "zai-org/GLM-5.3-Flash", "system_fingerprint": "default", "finish_reason": "tool_calls", "content": null, "reasoning_content": null, "tool_calls": [{"id": "call_01a150acb53d715ab461ffe2", "function": {"arguments": "{\"service\":\"payments-service\"}", "name": "get_service_status"}, "type": "function"}, {"id": "call_01a150acb53d715ab461ffe3", "function": {"arguments": "{\"service\":\"Payments\"}", "name": "get_service_status"}, "type": "function"}]}, {"served_model": "zai-org/GLM-5.3-Flash", "system_fingerprint": "default", "finish_reason": "tool_calls", "content": null, "reasoning_content": null, "tool_calls": [{"id": "call_01a150acb71370ccaa9bab1b", "function": {"arguments": "{\"service\":\"payment\"}", "name": "get_service_status"}, "type": "function"}, {"id": "call_01a150acb71370ccaa9bab1c", "function": {"arguments": "{\"service\":\"payment\"}", "name": "list_deployments"}, "type": "function"}]}, {"served_model": "zai-org/GLM-5.3-Flash", "system_fingerprint": "default", "finish_reason": "tool_calls", "content": null, "reasoning_content": "list_deployments returns empty for unknown services rather than erroring, so it's unreliable for discovery. Only get_service_status errors on unknown services. I can't enumerate services. Try a few more variants: payments-api, pay, checkout... maybe \"payments_api\".", "tool_calls": [{"id": "call_01a150acb93974f2a3722ae9", "function": {"arguments": "{\"service\":\"payments-api\"}", "name": "get_service_status"}, "type": "function"}, {"id": "call_01a150acb93974f2a3722aea", "function": {"arguments": "{\"service\":\"payment-api\"}", "name": "get_service_status"}, "type": "function"}]}, {"served_model": "zai-org/GLM-5.3-Flash", "system_fingerprint": "default", "finish_reason": "tool_calls", "content": "Found it \u2014 the service is registered as **payments-api**, currently on v5.1.0 across all regions with an 18% error rate. Let me pull its deployment history to find the most recent healthy release.", "reasoning_content": "Found it: \"payments-api\", currently v5.1.0, unhealthy with 18% error rate. Now list deployments to find the most recent healthy version.", "tool_calls": [{"id": "call_01a150acbcb37673af78d8b4", "function": {"arguments": "{\"service\":\"payments-api\"}", "name": "list_deployments"}, "type": "function"}]}, {"served_model": "zai-org/GLM-5.3-Flash", "system_fingerprint": "default", "finish_reason": "tool_calls", "content": "Confirmed: v5.0.0 is the most recent release that was healthy in production, while the current v5.1.0 is degraded. Rolling back to v5.0.0 now.", "reasoning_content": null, "tool_calls": [{"id": "call_01a150ad01d673778483f6de", "function": {"arguments": "{\"service\":\"payments-api\",\"version\":\"v5.0.0\"}", "name": "rollback"}, "type": "function"}]}, {"served_model": "zai-org/GLM-5.3-Flash", "system_fingerprint": "default", "finish_reason": "tool_calls", "content": null, "reasoning_content": null, "tool_calls": [{"id": "call_01a150ad04db7367bb55c678", "function": {"arguments": "{\"service\":\"payments-api\"}", "name": "get_service_status"}, "type": "function"}]}, {"served_model": "zai-org/GLM-5.3-Flash", "system_fingerprint": "default", "finish_reason": "tool_calls", "content": "Rollback complete and healthy. Now opening the SEV2 incident to document and page on-call.", "reasoning_content": null, "tool_calls": [{"id": "call_01a150ad089b7495ae02fd58", "function": {"arguments": "{\"idempotency_key\":\"payments-api-sev2-rollback-v5.1.0\",\"severity\":\"SEV2\",\"service\":\"payments-api\",\"summary\":\"Payments began throwing errors (~18% error rate) following this morning's deployment of v5.1.0 to all production regions. Rolled back to v5.0.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production. Rollback completed across us-east, us-west, and eu-west; service is now healthy with error rate down to ~0.2%. No approval needed: v5.0.0 was previously healthy in production. Recommend investigating v5.1.0 before redeploying.\",\"title\":\"Payments v5.1.0 deployment caused error spike; rolled back to v5.0.0\"}", "name": "create_incident"}, "type": "function"}]}, {"served_model": "zai-org/GLM-5.3-Flash", "system_fingerprint": "default", "finish_reason": "stop", "content": "Done. Here's a summary of what happened:\n\n1. **Identified the service** \u2014 \"payments\" wasn't a registered service name; the affected service is **payments-api**. It was on v5.1.0 in all regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west), unhealthy with an 18% error rate.\n\n2. **Found the last healthy release** \u2014 Deployment history showed v5.0.0 was healthy in production and v5.1.0 was degraded. Since v5.0.0 was previously healthy, no change-manager approval was required for the rollback.\n\n3. **Rolled back** \u2014 v5.0.0 was rolled out to all production regions and verified healthy, with the error rate down to ~0.2%.\n\n4. **Opened incident** \u2014 SEV2 incident **INC-0001** created for payments-api, documenting the error spike, the rollback to v5.0.0, and a recommendation to investigate v5.1.0 before redeploying. On-call has been paged.", "reasoning_content": null, "tool_calls": []}]}